ashville nashville has been a hot  destination for a while but i love it in  the summer because i think you get the  best of both worlds you get that  fun downtown nashville vibe with all the  music  you have the ryman you have so many  great things to do in the city but it's  also a great  base point for launching off into the  smoky mountains so you can get that  outdoor escape and hit some of those  wonderful destinations  the renaissance would be my pick for a  hotel you're right downtown in the heart  of the city you have a great  um bar restaurant scene right there  within your hotel  and lots of availability for this summer  as well and you're saying  if you really want to do a bucket list  place canada  is the place to be huh well look canada  is really not completely open yet but  where everybody i think you know that  really likes to head north to get kind  of that cooler weather is looking  forward to that so places like montreal  and toronto i say keep those on your  list and keep an eye out  for when those do reopen we're also  seeing that a lot of people are really  looking forward to  getting back to places like europe um  and people are already heading back  there this summer in fact marriott data  shows that  places like uh london paris rome munich  and madrid are really  kind of the hot places people are  looking to right now so  the good news for those international  travelers is that it is doable at this  point we love that you have so much  great information janine thank you so  much happy travels to you and jc  over to you
 

